      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f2718438-3bb4-5d20-8cf8-5b04a0205006",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eardwulf, Æthelred I, Ælfwald II, Æthelwald Moll, Æthelthryth, Alhred\n- Places: Northumbria\n- Concepts: kingship, dynastic strife, deposition, assassination\n\nFacts:\n- Æthelred I of Northumbria was born around 762 and was the son of Æthelwald Moll and Æthelthryth.\n- Æthelred I of Northumbria possibly became king while still a child after Alhred was deposed.\n- Æthelred I of Northumbria ruled Northumbria from 774 to 779.\n- In 790, during dynastic strife among several noble families in Northumbria, Æthelred I attempted to have Eardwulf assassinated.\n- Æthelred I of Northumbria ruled Northumbria again from 790 until he was murdered on 18 April 796.\n- Eardwulf of Northumbria may have had a second reign from 808 until perhaps 811 or 830.\n- According to one tradition, Ælfwald II reigned as king of Northumbria after Eardwulf was deposed in 806.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
